  ],
  "description": "Given a linked list, swap every two adjacent nodes and return its head. You must solve the problem without modifying the values in the list's nodes (i.e., only nodes themselves may be changed).",
  "pseudocode": "```javascript\n// 1. Initialize dummy node and pointers\nlet dummy = new ListNode(0);\ndummy.next = head;\nlet prev = dummy;\nlet curr = head;\n\n// 2. Iterate while there's a pair to swap\nwhile (curr !== null && curr.next !== null) {\n    // 3. Identify the nodes to be swapped\n    let firstNode = curr;\n    let secondNode = curr.next;\n\n    // 4. Perform the swap:\n    //    a. Link previous node to secondNode\n    prev.next = secondNode;\n    //    b. Link firstNode to the node after secondNode\n    firstNode.next = secondNode.next;\n    //    c. Link secondNode to firstNode\n    secondNode.next = firstNode;\n\n    // 5. Move pointers for the next iteration\n    prev = firstNode;\n    curr = firstNode.next;\n}\n\n// 6. Return the new head (dummy.next)\nreturn dummy.next;\n```",
